<title>RUSSIA: TENNIS-JOHANNSSON WINS ST.PETERSBURG OPEN.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-JOHANNSSON WINS ST.PETERSBURG OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PETERSBURG, Russia 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomas Johansson of Sweden beat Italian Renzo Furlan 6-3, 6-4 on Sunday to win the $300,000 St.Petersburg Open men's tennis tournament.</p>
<p>Johansson, 22, who beat favourite Michael Stich of Germany in the semifinals, said he was enjoying one of the best playing periods in his career.</p>
<p>&quot;The last two weeks are the best in my life,&quot; the fifth-seed Swede told a news conference. &quot;I have never played better than now.&quot;</p>
<p>Johansson won the first set easily, but Furlan put up a fight in the second, leading 4-3 until the Swede found his best service and outclassed the Italian.</p>
</text>
